{
  "id": "30018_tatemashi",
  "headword": "{建|た}て{増|ま}し",
  "reading": "たてまし",
  "romaji": "tatemashi",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "building extension; addition (to a house)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "building extension; addition (to a house)",
      "explanation": "Adding on to an existing building to enlarge it — an extra room, floor, or wing. The everyday counterpart of the more technical {増築|ぞうちく}. Takes する to mean to build such an addition."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30018_tatemashi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{部屋|へや}を{建|た}て{増|ま}しする。",
      "english": "To add on a room.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30018_tatemashi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}が{増|ふ}えたので、{家|いえ}を{建|た}て{増|ま}しした。",
      "english": "Since we had more children, we built an addition onto the house.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30018_tatemashi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{建|た}て{増|ま}しを{繰|く}り{返|かえ}した{結果|けっか}、{家|いえ}の{中|なか}が{迷路|めいろ}のようになってしまった。",
      "english": "As a result of repeated additions, the inside of the house ended up like a maze.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The everyday word for enlarging a house by building on. {増築|ぞうちく} is the more formal, technical term used on permits and in construction contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {部屋|へや}を{建|た}て{増|ま}しする: to add on a room\n- {建|た}て{増|ま}しを{繰|く}り{返|かえ}す: to keep adding on\n- {二階|にかい}を{建|た}て{増|ま}しする: to add a second floor\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {増築|ぞうちく}: extension/addition — the formal, technical equivalent\n- {改築|かいちく}: rebuilding/remodeling — reconstructing an existing structure, not enlarging it",
